tegrationProviderImpl(\n    Supplier<StsClient> stsClientSupplier,\n    Supplier<GoogleCredentials> gcpCredsProvider,\n    MetaStoreManagerFactory metaStoreManagerFactory) {   // NEW\n  this.stsClientSupplier = stsClientSupplier;\n  this.gcpCredsProvider = gcpCredsProvider;\n  this.metaStoreManagerFactory = metaStoreManagerFactory;\n  // ...rest unchanged\n}\n```\n\n**Change B (AZURE case, lines 93-101):** resolve the current realm from `CallContext` thread-local (the same pattern `TaskFileIOSupplier` uses at `TaskFileIOSupplier.java:54`), look up the per-realm cache, and pass it through:\n\n```java\ncase AZURE:\n  RealmContext realm = CallContext.getCurrentContext().getRealmContext();\n  AzureSecredCredentialCache secredCache =\n      metaStoreManagerFactory.getOrCreateAzureSecredCredentialCache(realm);\n\n  storageIntegration = (PolarisStorageIntegration<T>)\n      (credentialServiceRef.get() != null\n          ? new AzureCredentialsStorageIntegration(\n                catalogName,\n                credentialServiceRef,\n                credentialServiceFactory,\n                secredCache)                   // NEW\n          : new AzureCredentialsStorageIntegration());\n  break;\n```\n\nNote: `getStorageIntegrationForConfig` is called from `PolarisEclipseLinkMetaStoreSessionImpl.createStorageIntegration` / `loadPolarisStorageIntegration`, both of which run inside an established `CallContext` (set by the servlet filter or by bootstrap). Reading `CallContext.getCurrentContext()` inside this method is safe — this matches the `TaskFileIOSupplier` pattern.\n\n### 7. DI-site updates\n\nWherever `PolarisStorageIntegrationProviderImpl` is currently constructed (grep for `new PolarisStorageIntegrationProviderImpl(`), pass the `MetaStoreManagerFactory` reference. The factory instance is already available at DI time — it's what provides `storageIntegration` via `setStorageIntegrationProvider`, so the inverse reference just needs to be wired.\n\nIf you find a circular-depen