load. If false, every request \"\n                + \"fetches from SECRED directly (original pre-cache behavior).\")\n        .defaultValue(true)\n        .build();\n```\n\n**Step 2** — helper on `AzureCredentialsStorageIntegration` that checks the flag for the current call:\n\n```java\nprivate boolean isCacheEnabled() {\n  PolarisCallContext pc = CallContext.getCurrentContext().getPolarisCallContext();\n  return pc.getConfigurationStore().getConfiguration(pc, PolarisConfiguration.ENABLE_AZURE_SECRED_CACHE);\n}\n```\n\n**Step 3** — guard the two decision sites:\n\nIn `getOrFetchSecret()`:\n```java\nUnifiedDataLakeCredentials credential =\n    isCacheEnabled()\n        ? secredCredCache.getOrFetch(catalogName,\n              key -> fetchSecretWithRetry(key, credentialServiceRef, credentialServiceFactory))\n        : fetchSecretWithRetry(catalogName, credentialServiceRef, credentialServiceFactory);\n```\n\nIn the `ClientAuthenticationException` catch block inside `getSubscopedCreds`:\n```java\nif (secredCredCache != null\n    && catalogName != null\n    && isCacheEnabled()                      // NEW\n    && isInvalidClientSecretError(ex)\n    && !secredRefreshAttempted) {\n  // ...invalidate + refresh\n}\n```\n\n**Step 4** — to disable in a region, add to that region's Polaris YAML:\n\n```yaml\nfeatureConfiguration:\n  ENABLE_AZURE_SECRED_CACHE: false\n```\n\nRolling restart the Polaris deployment in that region. Done.\n\n## One thing to verify\n\nI don't know offhand whether `PolarisConfiguration` entries accept an all-uppercase key like `ENABLE_AZURE_SECRED_CACHE` or a dotted form like `polaris.azure.secred.cache.enabled`. Looking at the existing entries, they're all uppercase/underscore (`ALLOW_TABLE_LOCATION_OVERLAP`, `CLEANUP_ON_NAMESPACE_DROP`). Match that style.\n\n## Updated recommendation\n\nDrop the header-based approach (keep as an aside in the plan doc under \"alternatives considered\"), drop the `FeatureFlagsInspector` research thread for now (too much infrastructure for this PR), and use `PolarisConfiguration` + YAML. It's 15 lines of code change and fits the existing codebase conventions exactly.\n\nWant me to update the Configuration section of the plan doc to replace the header-based description with this approach?",
