            "new_string": "## Configuration\n\nGate the new behavior behind a feature flag so it can be disabled quickly if a regression surfaces in production. Two mechanisms are viable, in order of preference:\n\n1. **YAML via `PolarisConfiguration` + per-region deployment** (preferred, simplest, fits existing patterns).\n2. **HTTP-header-driven per-request flag** (stronger \"online toggle\" semantics; fallback if (1) is not sufficient).\n\nBoth are described below. Only one is needed — pick (1) unless there is a specific reason the deploy-to-flip cadence is too slow.\n\n### Mechanism 1: YAML-based flag via `PolarisConfiguration`\n\nPolaris has an existing typed flag registry in `polaris-core/src/main/java/org/apache/polaris/core/PolarisConfiguration.java`. Each `public static final PolarisConfiguration<T>` constant defines one flag — its key, description, default value, and optional catalog-level override name. The constants are consumed via `PolarisConfigurationStore.getConfiguration(callContext, flagConstant)`, which resolves the runtime value from the Dropwizard YAML config and falls back to the default if absent.\n\nExisting examples: `ALLOW_TABLE_LOCATION_OVERLAP`, `CLEANUP_ON_NAMESPACE_DROP`, `SUPPORTED_CATALOG_STORAGE_TYPES`. Our new flag follows the same shape.\n\nNote: on the Apache Polaris `polaris-1.0-main` branch, this class has been renamed to `FeatureConfiguration`. On the 0.9 branch we're on, it's still `PolarisConfiguration`. When merging upstream 1.0 later, the entry becomes a trivial rename.\n\n#### Why this gives region-scoped online control in Fivetran's deployment\n\n- Polaris runs as a separate deployment per region.\n- Each region owns its own YAML config (typically via k8s ConfigMap / Helm values).\n- To disable in region X: edit region X's YAML and trigger a rolling restart of that region's Polaris. Minutes, region-scoped, no coordination with upstream services needed.\n- Other regions remain on the old value.\n\nThe \"restart\" part is not meaningful friction at Fivetran's rollout cadence — the per-region deployment topology is what gives this mechanism its region-scoped online-toggle property.\n\n#### Flag entry\n\nAdd to `PolarisConfiguration.java`, following the style of the existing entries:\n\n```java\npublic static final PolarisConfiguration<Boolean> ENABLE_AZURE_SECRED_CACHE =\n    PolarisConfiguration.<Boolean>builder()\n        .key(\"ENABLE_AZURE_SECRED_CACHE\")\n        .description(\n            \"If true (default), Polaris caches Azure service principal credentials fetched \"\n                + \"from SECRED and uses the cache first to reduce SECRED load. If false, every \"\n                + \"request fetches from SECRED directly (original pre-cache behavior).\")\n        .defaultValue(true)\n        .build();\n```\n\n#### Helper in `AzureCredentialsStorageIntegration`\n\n```java\nprivate boolean isCacheEnabled() {\n  PolarisCallContext pc = CallContext.getCurrentContext().getPolarisCallContext();\n  return pc.getConfigurationStore()\n      .getConfiguration(pc, PolarisConfiguration.ENABLE_AZURE_SECRED_CACHE);\n}\n```\n\n#### Decision sites\n\n**Site 1 — `getOrFetchSecret()` initial load:**\n\n```java\nUnifiedDataLakeCredentials credential =\n    isCacheEnabled()\n        ? secredCredCache.getOrFetch(catalogName,\n              key -> fetchSecretWithRetry(key, credentialServiceRef, credentialServiceFactory))\n        : fetchSecretWithRetry(catalogName, credentialServiceRef, credentialServiceFactory);\n```\n\n**Site 2 — reactive invalidation path in `getSubscopedCreds()`:**\n\n```java\nif (secredCredCache != null\n    && catalogName != null\n    && isCacheEnabled()                      // NEW\n    && isInvalidClientSecretError(ex)\n    && !secredRefreshAttempted) {\n  // ...invalidate + refresh\n}\n```\n\nWhen the flag is off, every request goes directly to SECRED (pre-change behavior), and the reactive cache-refresh path becomes a no-op.\n\n#### To disable in a region\n\nAdd to that region's Polaris YAML:\n\n```yaml\nfeatureConfiguration:\n  ENABLE_AZURE_SECRED_CACHE: false\n```\n\nRoll the region's Polaris deployment. Done.\n\n#### Testing\n\nExtend `AzureCredentialsStorageIntegrationSpec` with a case using a stubbed `PolarisConfigurationStore` that returns `false` for `ENABLE_AZURE_SECRED_CACHE`. Assert that `secredCredCache.getOrFetch` is not invoked and `fetchSecretWithRetry` is called directly.\n\n---\n\n### Mechanism 2: HTTP-header-driven per-request flag",
